From ec6d034f7b1ca3749660efe80b092a294c74f4bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabriel FORTE <2580288+g4bwy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 23:59:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [Debug][Qwen4Exp] Unwire the PLE input_ids PP carry

A live probe (experiments/pp-inputids-probe.patch, 2026-10-20) compared
the wire copy against #61016's stage-local runner input_ids on every
eager forward: byte-identical on 768 consecutive real-traffic calls
(chunked prefill, mixed batches, MTP draft rows) on all three non-first
stages. The only observed mismatches were the fabricated warmup steps,
which read stale local buffers by construction and affect no serving
path.

Removes the input_ids staging buffer, the wire emit, and the consumer
shadow in both backend models; PLE now uses the runner argument every
stage already has. Tests retargeted: intermediate tensors must never
carry ids, and non-first ranks feed the stage-local tensor to layers.
Guard deletions from patch 2 remain (upstream #56444 still open).

Candidate for shrinking series patch 2; pending boot cert.
